{"id": "sevt_01CAKdvMemihoFcPj4voqwcG", "content": [{"text": "The evidence is consistent end-to-end. Here's the triage.\n\n## Checkout 500s \u2014 triage\n\n**Timeline**\n- **14:31:18** \u2014 checkout deploy `a3f9c21` (\"refactor order summary builder for readability\").\n- **14:31** \u2014 checkout p99 jumps **75ms \u2192 ~3,900ms** in the same minute as the deploy.\n- **14:31 \u2192 14:40** \u2014 `db_pool_utilization` ramps steadily **0.20 \u2192 1.0** (pool pegged at 100%).\n- **14:40** \u2014 first 500 appears (`error=PoolTimeout`); error_rate climbs to 0.2\u20130.6.\n\n**Mechanism (from the diff)**\n`build_summary` used to do one batched query and group in memory:\n```python\nall_items = OrderItem.objects.filter(order_id__in=ids)   # 1 query\n```\nThe refactor moved it to a per-order query inside the loop:\n```python\nfor order in rows:\n    items = OrderItem.objects.filter(order_id=order.order_id)  # 1 query PER row\n```\nThat's a classic **N+1**.\n\n**Log confirmation**\n- 3,320 `SELECT * FROM order_items WHERE order_id = ?` single-row queries after the deploy (none before).\n- 268 checkout requests fanning out to **8\u201316 queries each** (median 12).\n- 70 checkout 500s, all `at/after 14:31`, zero before; all are `error=PoolTimeout` on `/api/checkout/validate`.\n\nEach request now holds many more connections for longer \u2192 pool saturates (util = 1.0 by 14:40) \u2192 requests that can't grab a connection error out with PoolTimeout \u2192 500s.\n\n**Fix:** revert/patch `a3f9c21` to restore the batched `order_id__in` query (and drop the per-row debug log).\n\n> **Root cause:** `a3f9c21` \u2014 the order-summary refactor replaced a single batched `order_id__in` query with a per-row query (N+1), saturating the checkout DB connection pool and causing PoolTimeout 500s.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T04:50:00.545598Z", "type": "agent.message"}
